{number: 117}
{title: Hail to the Brightness}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] Hail to the brightness of Zion's glad [G7] morning,
[C] Joy to the lands that in [F] darkness have [C] lain!
Hushed be the [G7] accents of [C] sorrow and [G7] mourning,
[C] Zion in triumph be-[F] gins her mild [C] reign.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[C] Hail to the brightness of Zion's glad [G7] morning,
[C] Long by the prophets of [F] Israel fore-[C] told;
Hail to the [G7] millions from [C] bondage re-[G7] turning!
[C] Gentiles and Jews the blest [F] vision be-[C] hold.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[C] Lo, in the desert rich flowers are [G7] springing,
[C] Streams ever copious are [F] gliding a-[C] long;
Loud from the [G7] mountain tops [C] echoes are [G7] ringing,
[C] Wastes rise in verdure and [F] mingle in [C] song.
{end_of_verse}
